  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C62-repaso-gerundio",
      "sequence": 2435,
      "title": "(review)",
      "headword": "(review)",
      "romanization": "(review)",
      "gloss": "two endings and one little a — the smallest new machinery in this book, and one of the most useful",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:0a3444b4cadb4ae4",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two endings, three families. (-ando for -ar; -iendo for everything else.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three chants."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First. Hablando, comiendo, viviendo. — one form each, no agreement, no persons. The smallest thing this book has asked of you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second. Estoy comiendo. — estar carries the person, the gerund never moves. And it means now: for tomorrow you still say voy a comer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third. Veo a María, but veo la casa. — the little a in front of a person, and nothing in front of a house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: both of these are Latin's absence",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The gerund is what is left of a Latin form after its case endings fell off — which is why it has exactly one shape and agrees with nothing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The personal a is what grew back because case endings fell off. Latin marked the receiving end with an ending; Spanish marks it with a preposition, but only where it matters, which is people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One rule is a leftover and the other is a repair. Same cause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the three chants, in order",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the three chants, in order]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C62-repaso-gerundio-now",
              "prompt": "Say: we are studying.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-PROGRESSIVE-ESTAR-GERUND"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 13,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "estamos estudiando",
                "estamos estudiando."
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Estar moves; the gerund stands still.",
                "incorrect": "Estamos estudiando."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C62-repaso-gerundio-a",
              "prompt": "Which of these takes the little a -- seeing a house, or seeing a person?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-PERSONAL-A"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "a person",
                "seeing a person"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "People only.",
                "incorrect": "A person."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C62-repaso-gerundio-tomorrow",
              "prompt": "How do you say you are eating with somebody tomorrow?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-PROGRESSIVE-NOT-FUTURE"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 14,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "voy a comer",
                "with voy a comer, not estoy comiendo"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "The progressive cannot reach tomorrow.",
                "incorrect": "Voy a comer -- the progressive means now."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many gerund endings? (Two.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And which of this chapter's two rules is a repair rather than a leftover? (The personal a — it grew to replace a lost ending.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
